From 5c7417fc5585c2dd08256d9bff302226e940757c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mi210 <mi210@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 03:26:25 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] hip: Inkling-2 decode fusions round 2 (mix, short conv)

- mix: concat chain + rms_norm + transpose copy + query repeat + score
  GEMV + softmax in one kernel (one block per state, last block does the
  scores/softmax; per-call-site ticket counters). nq <= 2 only: the
  3-query case does not reproduce mul_mat_vec_f<.., 3, ..> bit for bit.
- sconv: concat + state store + ssm_conv + add + scale, decided at the
  CONCAT and launched at the SSM_CONV (deferred skip set). When the conv
  history is no longer intact at the SSM_CONV (FFN conv), the concat and
  state store run at the CONCAT and the rest at the SSM_CONV.
  Early/late placement is guarded by memory-overlap checks over every
  node in between (views and empty tensors ignored).
- backend loop: ggml_cuda_inkling_should_skip + negative try_fuse result
  for "node handled".
Kernels per decoded token 7243 -> 3497; tg128 33.4 -> 44.8 tok/s;
kld.sh logits md5 identical to baseline; llama-server greedy outputs
identical (6/6, also with DSpark).

